 "source_type": "instagram",
 "source_url": "https://www.instagram.com/reel/Db3Xjr8saru/",
 "title": "Dealing with the Overwhelm of Learning",
 "topic": "mindset",
 "summary": "The creator discusses the feeling of being overwhelmed when realizing how much there is to learn in the world. She explains that the paradox of curiosity is that the more you learn, the more you realize you do not know, and advises that you do not need to know everything at once.",
 "key_points": [
  "Researching one topic can suddenly reveal fifty other things you know nothing about.",
  "The paradox of curiosity is that the more curious you become, the more you realize how little you actually know.",
  "You will never know everything, get through every book, or master every skill.",
  "Allow yourself to be fascinated by things because it is part of a personality that wants to learn and expand.",
  "You do not need to understand every bit of a concept; just constantly keep finding something worth learning."
 ],
 "content": "curiosity didn’t kill the cat because it didn’t get overwhelmed\nDo you ever just sit down to work and suddenly get overwhelmed with how much there is to learn? That you just shut everything and immediately start scrolling reels the next second? Like you start researching one thing and suddenly realize there are 50 other things you know nothing about. And then you realize there's so much knowledge out there, like so many books you haven't read, things you still don't understand. And weirdly, that thought can make you want to learn everything at once or just close your laptop and doom scroll for 3 hours straight. Because the paradox is, the more curious you become, the more you realize how little you actually know. And I've realized that is not something to be overwhelmed by. Maybe that's the point, because you'll never know everything. You'll never get through every book or master every skill. So you have to let yourself be fascinated by things because that's part of a personality that wants to constantly learn and expand. Sometimes a little reminder would be nice that you don't need to understand every bit of a concept. You just need to constantly keep finding something worth learning.\nText shown on screen: curiosity didn’t kill the cat because it didn’t get overwhelmed",
 "status": "done",
